CORE
intra_vector_slices1.sv
--ic3
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.v == 228: PROVED$
^\[main\.p1\] always main\.w == \{ 4 \{ main\.x \} \}: PROVED$
^\[main\.p2\] always main\.y == \{ main\.a, main\.a \}: PROVED$
^\[main\.p3\] always main\.z == 228: PROVED$
^\[main\.p4\] always main\.u\[1:0\] == 2'b01: PROVED$
^\[main\.p5\] always main\.u\[3:2\] == 2'b00: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p6\] always main\.t == 2'b00: REFUTED$
^\[main\.p7\] always main\.r\[3:2\] == 2'b00: PROVED$
^\[main\.p8\] always main\.arr\[0\] == 2'b01: PROVED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
As intra_vector_slices1.desc, with the IC3 engine, which uses the netlist.
Continuous assignments to slices of a vector may read other slices of the
same vector. Only slices that depend on themselves, directly or through
other slices of the vector, are combinational loops, and only those are
treated as non-deterministic.
